each file lands in your folder under its name, and its `fetched:` line names its /cdn/ address, the one the world uses. With no `fetched:` line below, `spawn tripo status 991f4b4c-c4a1-4257-bbbd-899ae6da5bd2 --out robot-frame.glb` lands them.
facing: a workshop file, so it faces the way its bytes do: Tripo puts the side that robot-frame.generated_image_url.jpeg shows on +X. Set model.forward to where the subject faces there: toward you "+x", away "-x", to the picture's left "+z", to its right no forward.
